  "blocks": [
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Clone naming"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "When cloning drives or whole servers the paramater for the name of the cloned entity could be omitted. In that scenario clone naming strategy based on the profile settings is being invoked."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Clone naming strategies are kept on clone_naming property in the user profile object. Possible values for it:"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "NONE do not append anything to the cloned drive’s name. [default]"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "COUNTER appends a number at the end of the name or increase it in case there is a number already."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "DATE appends the current date or try to update it in case there is one already."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "TIMESTAMP appends the current timestamp or try to update it in case there is one already."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "clone-naming",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "If the date/timestamp at the end is already up-to-date the clone naming strategy will fallback to COUNTER without stripping the date/timestamp before."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "example",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Example"
    },
